All buildings or structures within the corporate limits of the city which have any or all of the following defects shall be deemed to be unsafe buildings:
(1) Buildings which, exclusive of the foundation, show 33 percent or more, of damage or deterioration of the supporting member or members, or 50 percent of damage or deterioration of a nonsupporting enclosing or outside walls or covering;
(2) Buildings which have improperly distributed loads upon the floors or roofs, or in which the same are overloaded, or which have insufficient strength to be reasonably safe for the purpose for which it is used, or intended to be used;
(3) Buildings which have been damaged by fire, wind, or other causes, so as to have become dangerous to life or the general health and welfare of the occupants thereof, or the people of the city;
(4) Buildings which have become or are so dilapidated, decayed, unsafe, unsanitary, or which so utterly fail to provide the amenities essential to decent living that they are unfit for human habitation, or are likely to cause sickness or disease, so as to work injury to the health, safety, or general welfare of those living therein, or may live therein;
(5) Those having light, air and sanitation facilities which are inadequate to protect the health, safety, or general welfare of human beings who live or may live therein;
(6) Buildings which have inadequate facilities for egress in case of fire or panic, or those having insufficient stairways, elevators, fire escapes, or other means of communication;
(7) Buildings which have parts thereof which are so attached that they may fall and injure members of the public or property;
(8) Buildings which, because of their condition, are unsafe, unsanitary, or dangerous to the health, safety, or general welfare of the people of the city;
(9) Buildings which exist in violation of any provision of the building code of this city, or any provisions of the fire prevention code or any other ordinance of the city, so as to constitute a nuisance, and to be unsafe, unsanitary, or dangerous to the health, safety, or general welfare of the people of the city.
(Prior Code, § 15.12.010; Ord. No. 548, § 1, 5-12-1980)

